      "message": "I\u0027m afraid those values were already wrong for STM32F091VC used in oak derivatives.\nie STM32F091VC has 256kB flash with 32 protection regions (31 x 4kB + 1 x 132kB)\nright now it declares:\nCONFIG_FLASH_SIZE 0x00040000    /* \u003d 256kB */\nCONFIG_FLASH_BANK_SIZE  0x2000  /* \u003d 8kB !!! */\nso that\u0027s PHYSICAL_BANKS \u003d 32 (which is right)\nbut we have 31 4kB banks and 1 132kB bank (rather than 32x 8kB banks)\n\nso IMO all the computations above are questionably correct for that particular case \nand you are adding one more wrong one ;-)\n\nFor your work, that\u0027s probably not a terribly interesting corner case but probably you should at least add a bug number here to try avoid people to fall later into this trap too badly.\nI have opened crosbug.com/p/62372 with some details",
